# Environment template for prometheus-community/yet-another-cloudwatch-exporter v0.67.0
# https://github.com/prometheus-community/yet-another-cloudwatch-exporter
#
# Copy to yace.env (gitignored) and fill in real values, or render via your secrets manager.
# NEVER commit the copy with real values.
#
# Credentials use the AWS SDK default credential chain — this file does not set static AWS
# keys. Pick ONE of the options below depending on how the host authenticates to AWS.
# https://aws.github.io/aws-sdk-go-v2/docs/configuring-sdk/#specifying-credentials

# Option A (recommended): EC2 instance profile / ECS task role / EKS IRSA — no variables needed.
# Leave AWS_SHARED_CREDENTIALS_FILE and AWS_PROFILE unset.

# Option B: shared credentials file (useful for local Docker Compose validation only).
# Point at a file OUTSIDE this repo (or a gitignored path); it must not be committed.
# AWS_SHARED_CREDENTIALS_FILE=/etc/yace/aws-credentials
# AWS_PROFILE=default

# Option C: cross-account role assumption is configured in exporters/yace/config.yml (roleArn),
# not via environment variables.

# Region used for STS calls when assuming roles (optional; only needed for cross-account setups).
# AWS_STS_REGION=us-east-1

# Uncomment to point the AWS SDK at a local stub (e.g. moto/localstack) for offline validation.
# AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=http://localhost:4566
